[h1]CursorBridge | Stellaris Cursor Size · Live 1–96 px[/h1]
Make the game cursor smaller when it covers information, or larger when you need more visibility. Choose the size that fits your screen with a live slider.

[b]This Workshop mod requires the free CursorBridge companion program. Subscribing alone does not resize the cursor.[/b]

[h2]Download the companion[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/shenbo1264/cursorbridge/releases/tag/v0.9.4]GitHub Release — download the Windows x64 build[/url]
[url=https://github.com/shenbo1264/cursorbridge/releases/download/v0.9.4/CursorBridge.exe]Direct single-file EXE download[/url]
[url=https://github.com/shenbo1264/cursorbridge]Source code, README and issue tracker[/url]

These links lead directly to this project's GitHub page or Release asset. No file-hosting ads, shorteners or third-party redirect pages. SHA256 sums are included. The initial binary is unsigned; open source enables inspection and rebuilding, not a security guarantee.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Live 1–96 pixel resizing in one-pixel steps.
[*]Exact input and keyboard controls; 12 original arrow/crosshair/ring sets in four palettes.
[*]Three saved presets, game-scoped hotkeys and optional confinement released on focus loss.
[*]Start with 24–32 px. 1 px is an extreme small option; 96 px is available for large-pointer needs and demonstrations.
[*]Keeps the installed game's artwork, hotspots and existing animated cursors.
[*]Restore the original cursor anytime; keep the chosen size after closing the panel.
[*]Chinese UI for Chinese game settings, English for other languages.
[*]Windows desktop pointer preferences remain unchanged.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe and enable this mod in the launcher.
[*]Download CursorBridge.exe from the GitHub Release and double-click; no manual extraction or separate DLL is needed.
[*]Start Stellaris normally. The companion detects the game, or lets you select stellaris.exe through its tray menu.
[*]Choose “Open live slider” in the single-player startup event, or use the free “Cursor size settings” edict.
[*]Drag to adjust; restore from the panel or tray whenever needed.
[/olist]

Start the companion before using the event, or reopen the edict after connecting. You can also use the tray panel without this mod.

[h2]Compatibility and limits[/h2]
The first public test release targets Windows x64 / Stellaris 4.5.1. Scripts are marked for 4.5.*; the in-game bridge currently supports single-player only.

The core adds uniquely named scripts and does not overwrite 00_on_actions.txt, the tech tree or a full GUI. It was smoke-tested with UOD + Dark Blue UI; other combinations still need specific checks. The script mod affects the checksum. Achievements and multiplayer compatibility are not promised.

The live slider is a floating companion panel. An optional, locally generated settings-page button can be built for the player's installed UI. It is not shipped in this core Workshop package and must be regenerated after UI updates.

[h2]Open source and future work[/h2]
Original CursorBridge code and themes are MIT licensed. Version 0.7 includes shapes/colors, presets, hotkeys and optional confinement. More adapters, user pack import, an editor and overlay effects remain future work. The project's feature comparison documents exactly what is implemented and verified.

Independently developed; not affiliated with Paradox Interactive, Steam or YoloMouse. No original game cursor assets are bundled and no game files need to be replaced.
